1
00:00,000 --> 00:08,000
This is a planetary gearbox. It is simulated at the atomic
scale and at the device scale. The sun gear turns. The
planets turn. The carrier turns.

2
00:08,000 --> 00:19,000
nano-cad is a multiscale design tool. It has five model
levels. Only L1, the atomistic engine, and L2, the device
layer, are implemented. L0, L3, and L4 are later work.

3
00:19,000 --> 00:29,000
A clean checkout reproduces the whole demo with one
command. The first run needs network access. It downloads
the build and test tools.

4
00:29,000 --> 00:40,000
Every force term has a finite-difference gradient test.
Every integrator has an energy-conservation test. The
tests are a merge gate, not a phase.

5
00:40,000 --> 00:52,000
The agent calls typed tools. It never edits coordinates.
It asks for a planetary set with three planets. The
generator returns the atoms and the bonds.

6
00:52,000 --> 01:02,000
The agent assembles the L2 device. The device has seven
bodies and six joints. The constraints are position-level
projections.

7
01:02,000 --> 01:12,000
The agent drives the sun and measures the sun-to-carrier
ratio. The analytic ratio is three point five. The
simulated ratio is three point five. The relative error is
one point one four six times ten to the minus ten.

8
01:12,000 --> 01:22,000
The agent exports a URDF with seven links and six joints.
The scene export carries three layers: atomistic, device,
and coarse. A viewer animates across them.

9
01:22,000 --> 01:28,000
Six hundred atoms. Serial: six hundred eighty
microseconds. Four workers: three hundred seventy-one.

10
01:28,000 --> 01:30,000
All results are simulated.
